Package: asdcontrol
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: brightness control for Apple Studio Display and Pro Display XDR
 asdcontrol reads and sets the brightness of an Apple Studio Display or an
 Apple Pro Display XDR connected over USB-C, by talking to the display's
 USB HID interface through a /dev/usb/hiddev* or /dev/hiddev* device node.
 Those nodes are owned by root, so the program is normally run with sudo.
 .
 This package ships /etc/sudoers.d/50-asdcontrol, which lets members of the
 sudo group run the detect, read and set invocations of asdcontrol without
 a password. The Oaxaca desktop's oaxaca-brightness-display-apple
 script relies on that rule.
